  "body": "Two linked setup-page alignment changes on one branch. Both edit the same alignment picks, so they would conflict as separate PRs. The fork is synced at v0.15.0; branched with upstream/main merged.\n\n## #557: set the part's X and Y in the work plane by an edge or two points (`bc2f5353`)\n- **App** (`pick/axis.rs`, `turn_in_plane`):\n  - **Pick:** an `AxisPick`, one straight edge or two vertices plus a flip, is read through the setup's current part alignment, so it composes after a face-to-plane lay.\n  - **Turn:** the pick is projected onto the setup's XY, and the part turns about setup Z around its centre, so it stays on its spot of the table.\n  - **Both axes:** the primary one (Y by default, or X) is laid exactly. The other is only checked: a parallel or left-handed pair is refused, never averaged.\n  - **One axis:** the other follows right-handed (X = Y × Z).\n  - **Precision:** quarter turns snap exactly.\n- **Command:** the existing undoable `AlignPartToSetup` (new `turn_in_plane` / `check_turn` entries). The stock follows, linked setups follow, ops go stale and undo clears that. The same `part_alignment` field is used, so there is **no project-file change**.\n- **Refused by name:** a face, a closed or curved edge, a single point, coincident points, an edge mixed with a point, a pick that isn't the part, a stale pick, a direction within 5° of the plane normal, a parallel or left-handed X/Y, nothing picked, a non-finite result, and \"already holds the part that way\".\n- **UI:** a new \"Axes in the plane - pick an edge or two points for +Y and/or +X\" section on the setup page and the Setups overview.\n  - Per axis: by Edge or by Two points, a Pick toggle, and Flip.\n  - Then Primary, **Apply axes** (greyed with the reason; it shows the turn in degrees first) and Clear.\n- **MCP:** `set_part_axes`.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/557-axis-by-edge.md`.\n\n## #554: the setup page's plane alignment picks faces only (`7d641c8b`)\n- **Plane row:** it now reads \"Lay on a plane - pick a face\" and arms Face mode, so a click beside an edge takes the face.\n- **Removed:** the #330 two-edge plane mode. `pick::lay_on_plane` refuses an edge by name (\"an edge cannot set a plane; pick a flat face (edges set an axis: Axes in the plane)\").\n- **Unchanged:** 3-2-1 alignment and operation-geometry edge picks.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/554-plane-pick-faces-only.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **App `axis_align` (10):**\n  - an edge at 30° → +Y, about the centre;\n  - two points as X;\n  - flip;\n  - both axes, Y or X primary, plus the left-handed and parallel refusals;\n  - a tilted pick projects cleanly;\n  - near-normal and degenerate picks, a curved arc and a closed rim are refused;\n  - undo and redo;\n  - composes after a face lay;\n  - stale, and undo clears it.\n- **MCP:** `set_part_axes_turns_the_part_from_an_edge_or_two_points`.\n- **UI:**\n  - `setup_axis_tests` (3): edge → Apply → undo and redo, with a face refused; two points plus flip; an upright edge greys Apply with the reason.\n  - New `plane_face_pick`: a real viewport click 4 px inside a face takes the face with the plane row armed, and the edge with an axis row armed.\n  - `structural`: `setup_page_alignment_rows_structure`.\n- **Updated:** `plane_align`, `plane_align_edges`, `winding_align` and `setup_plane_tests`, whose two-edge cases now expect the edge refusal (plus `every_edge_pick_is_refused_by_name`).\n- **Gate:** setup_align, plane_align(_edges), winding_align, wcs_align, commands_undo, project_roundtrip, mcp, mcp_setup, mcp_pick, setup_relative and setup_carry pass, as do the ui boundary_picks and edge_loop_pick tests. ui lib passes 381 of 382; the one failure, the headless-GPU test, comes from the machine. Clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\nA hands-on GUI check. The axis rows' clicks are fed to the draft in tests; the face/edge routing is pinned through a real viewport click.\n\n**Deferred:**\n- \"Two points\" takes model vertices only, not face centroids or typed coordinates.\n- The work plane is always the setup's XY.\n\n**Merge note:** #554 is a fix, but it rides with a feat, so this PR merges at the cut. If the fix is wanted sooner, `7d641c8b` can be split out.\n\nChangelog: Setup alignment: set the part's +Y / +X in the work plane by picking a straight edge or two points (flip, Y or X primary), composed after a face-to-plane lay; one undoable step; MCP set_part_axes (#557)\nChangelog: Setup page plane alignment picks faces only - a click beside an edge takes the face; the two-edge plane mode is removed and an edge is refused by name (#554)\n\nFixes #557\nFixes #554\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
